// PLAYBOOK RULESET: ADTECH STANDARD TERMS (V3.1)
// Priority: High

Rule_101 [REJECT_CLAUSE]: Any clause establishing exclusive jurisdiction or governing law outside of California (Company HQ) or New York (Primary Operations) is strictly prohibited for contracts exceeding $100,000 in value. No fallback language exists; such clauses must be rejected and the vendor instructed to remove the provision entirely before re-submission.

Rule_102 [NEGOTIATE_REDLINE]: For contracts under $100,000, governing law may be negotiated to the vendor's state if accompanied by a mutual jury trial waiver.

Rule_103 [ESCALATE_TO_COUNSEL]: If the clause mentions 'Delaware' specifically, check Rule_101 first. If Rule_101 applies, do not escalate; reject. Escalation is only for ambiguous jurisdiction clauses not covered by Rule_101 or 102.

Rule_104 [ACCEPT_AS_IS]: Clauses specifying California or New York law.

